 "result": "Fixed `PackageLoader.list_templates()` for zip packages on Python 3.13. CPython 3.13 renamed `zipimporter._files` (an attribute) to `zipimporter._get_files()` (a method), which was silently making the loader raise `TypeError` for all 3.13 zip-package users, not just PyPy as the old xfail assumed.\n\nChanges:\n- `src/jinja2/loaders.py`: `list_templates()` now checks for `_get_files()` first (3.13+), falls back to `_files` (older CPython), and still raises `TypeError` only for implementations lacking both (PyPy).\n- `tests/test_loader.py`: narrowed the `xfail` on `test_package_zip_list` to PyPy only, since 3.13 is now fully supported.\n- `CHANGES.rst`: noted the fix.\n\nVerified `tests/test_loader.py` (all 41 tests) passes on both Python 3.11 and 3.13.",
